1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,240
In this video, we're going to look at configuring your BurpSuite Enterprise Edition web server.

2
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:15,000
After installation, we recommend setting up the web server URL. This is used by many of the features

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,880
in BurpSuite Enterprise, such as when links sent by email are generated and when password reset

4
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:28,920
links are created. To configure this, go to the settings menu and choose network. Enter either

5
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:34,200
the fully qualified domain name or IP address of the machine where the web server is installed,

6
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:40,200
and make sure to include the port number. You can come back and change these settings later on

7
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:45,080
on standard deployments. If you do change them though, you would need to wait for the web server

8
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:51,960
to restart and then log in again. If you have a Kubernetes deployment, you cannot change the web

9
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:56,520
server ports as your external port should be configured as part of your ingress solution setup.

10
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:04,200
By default, when using the embedded database, the web server is configured to use unencrypted HTTP.

11
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:11,000
So we recommend enabling TLS for production use so your traffic is encrypted. To do this,

12
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,160
you will need to ensure you have a certificate with a .p12 file extension. Select the use TLS switch

13
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:21,640
and when prompted upload your certificate. Enter the password for the certificate file

14
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:32,920
and you also have the option to enable HSTS. If you've already configured your web server URL at the stage

15
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:38,840
where you enable HTTPS, you will also need to update this in your web server URL.

16
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:45,640
You can now start using your new settings.

